  "raw": " seven months.\n\nBen Davies, Cabinet Member for Regeneration and Transport, said: “We thought this would be resolved. Despite talking to them it’s still in dispute and it needs resolving urgently as they have not paid their rent.\n\n“Coventry Airport has told us that they have adequate numbers of passengers flying here but agreements were available from 2016 (rather than 2014) so these should have been resolved then.\n\nCurrently it is proving very difficult to lease further hangar space given the huge amount of overall demand across the CAA and elsewhere and there are also issues with whether existing tenders have been released or how often new ones will form part of plans for development in the harbour area. Again we are trying to find ways forward on both accounts. The reality seems to be that demand has outstripped supply meaning everyone involved must work much harder - and potentially here for quite some time yet considering Legacy in particular can take up to 12 years! There were limits",
  "serialized": "seven months. Ben Davies, Cabinet Member for Regeneration and Transport, said: “We thought this would be resolved. Despite talking to them it’s still in dispute and it needs resolving urgently as they have not paid their rent. “Coventry Airport has told us that they have adequate numbers of passengers flying here but agreements were available from 2016 (rather than 2014) so these should have been resolved then. Currently it is proving very difficult to lease further hangar space given the huge amount of overall demand across the CAA and elsewhere and there are also issues with whether existing tenders have been released or how often new ones will form part of plans for development in the harbour area. Again we are trying to find ways forward on both accounts. The reality seems to be that demand has outstripped supply meaning everyone involved must work much harder - and potentially here for quite some time yet considering Legacy in particular can take up to 12 years! There were limits",
